{"game": "deep-rock-galactic", "language": "english", "appid": 548430, "month": "2021-07", "window": 3, "start_date": 1626393600, "end_date": 1627084799, "month_true_total": 2033, "quota": 5, "returned": 5, "pulled_at": "2026-08-29 21:22:58 Pacific Daylight Time", "reviews": [{"recommendationid": "96263919", "author": {"steamid": "76561198065307024", "personaname": "Jorako", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/Jorako/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 7, "playtime_forever": 35286, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 10492, "last_played": 1767037755, "avatar": "be17b15e02921dd1b6095eb157bf8849597bef32"}, "language": "english", "review": "Everyone's experience will differ, but this is a game best played with friends...\nTo give context to my experience, my preferred class was the driller class.\nI played with a friend that played scout, he would always shout at me to drill for minerals, or to go to whichever point, and it aggravated me that I could never see what he meant until a lot of searching... I would also get really bad fits of nausea while playing for too long.\n\nIt turns out, he was playing on an ultra-wide monitor with the highest mobility class...\nI was playing on a CRT with 4:3 resolution... I WAS PLAYING WITH TUNNEL VISION THIS WHOLE TIME!!!\nIt does a difference in this game, with your FOV anyhow, lesson learned.\n\n10/10 would play a driller with tunnel vision again.\n(I have a newer monitor with a high refresh rate to avoid nausea now, not ultra-wide, but 16:9, it really does make a difference. I still see less then my scout friend, but I like the default FOV. Don't play on a 4:3 CRT unless you're a real minor without nausea anyhow lol!)", "timestamp_created": 1627084509, "timestamp_updated": 1627084509, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 1, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.504357337951660156", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "